  The reel_script says the road is 'வசந்தபுரம் – லத்துவாடி – வள்ளிபுரம்' built in 'ஐந்து கட்டங்களாக' — the article says the 5 stages are Namakkal-Mudalaipatti to Vallipuram; the 103 crore road is stages 4 and 5 only, so the reel_script's framing mixes the 197 crore project with the 103 crore stretch in one sentence.
  The reel_script states the 197 crore ring road project was 'அறிவிக்கப்பட்டு' and then that the Vasanthapuram–Lathuvadi–Vallipuram road is built at 103 crore, mixing two different cost figures/projects in adjacent sentences without clarity.
  The reel_script says 'கடந்த ஜனவரி மாதம்' for the foundation stone, which the article gives only as 'கடந்த ஜன.,யில' (January) — month name is consistent, but the year is not stated, so no year error; however the reel_script omits that the road is handled by the Tamil Nadu State Highways Department (தமிழ்நாடு மாநில நெடுஞ்சாலைத்துறை) and the 'விரிவான சாலை உள்கட்டமைப்பு மேம்பாட்டு திட்டம்' scheme, which is an important fact of the article.
  The reel_script omits the fact that the ring road is meant to ease traffic congestion for vehicle drivers who are struggling (விழிபிதுங்குகின்றனர) — minor, but the reel_script omits the 'ஐந்து கட்டமாக' detail's stage names (Namakkal-Mudalaipatti New Bus Stand to Vallipuram), which are important route facts.
